

    CDS_Setup.rexx     A config file compiler for CDScroller

While attempting to setup CDScroller with TransAmiga, I found that all the
fiddly little bits involved in making up each CD's config files was
probably better spent doing more enjoyable things, and as Urban Mueller
(Aminet) is now releasing 4 Aminet CDs each year, setting up each new
edition can be a tedius task.

With all that in mind, I set about writing an ARexx script to build the
config files for each new Aminet CD automagically. CDS_Setup.rexx is it.

If you have CDScroller running, you'll know about the little fiddly
programs supplied with it to build each new CD's config file.

CDS_Setup.rexx is designed to do away with all of those.

   Running CDS_Setup.rexx

To run CDS_Setup.rexx, you'll firstly need to edit the config section at
the top of the script. This consists of ONE (1) whole variable, the
destination directory for your CDScroller configs. (hard work that!)

The destination directory that you've added to the script must exist on
your system and inside said directory, you should move the TREE file
(supplied)


**** IMPORTANT ****

This TREE file is a compilation of every directory that does or has
existed on Aminet up until now. If the script fails in the next section,
it's probably because the new CD you're adding contains a directory which
isn't listed in the supplied file. ****** BE WARNED! ******

*******************

Then, simply insert the CD from which you want to draw the configs into
your CD drive and type into a shell window "rx CDS_Setup.rexx <CDName>"

You'll see lots of files being written to your designated area, along with
new directories being created. Lastly, CDS_Setup.rexx will build the file
DIRS.TXT inside the configured directory and copy the CD's INDEX file
across as well. (needed for filename searching)

From there, you should have a complete configuration for the new Aminet
CD, except for the name and description in the file CD.config which will
have to be added manually. (I tried to automate this bit as well, but as
it's Christmas Day, I want SOME time to myself)


A typical finished directory structure would look like this....

File:CD/--------TREE (file)
      |
     Aminet26
      |    |
      |    Aminet
      |      |
      |      |------------------------------------biz
      |      |----------------comm                 |--cloan-Files.BBS
      |      |-demo             |--amiex-Files.BBS |--dbase-Files.BBS
      |      | |--aga-Files.BBS |--bbs---Files.BBS |--demo--Files.BBS
   DIRS.TXT  | |--ecs-Files.BBS |--cnet--Files.BBS |--dopus-Files.BBS
    INDEX    |
   (files)

You get the picture! 8^)

CDS_Setup.rexx has been tested on Aminet CDs 4, 7, 8 and 14-26 on an Amiga
2000/060@50Mhz. I doubt that it will work on CDs other than those released
by Aminet.

Have fun.

